{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":40.7400016784668,"text":"In the Earth Hall, beside the Exhibition Road entrance, stands a real Stegosaurus skeleton, 5.6 metres long, with big plates along its back and four spikes on its tail. It was found in Wyoming in America in 2003 and is the most complete Stegosaurus in the world. Almost 300 of its bones are its own, not copies. The museum named it Sophie, after the daughter of the man who helped buy it, although nobody knows whether the animal was a boy or a girl. It was young when it died, 150 million years ago, so it had not grown as big as it could have.","words":[{"word":"In","start":0,"end":0.46000000834465027},{"word":"the","start":0.46000000834465027,"end":0.699999988079071},{"word":"Earth","start":0.699999988079071,"end":1.0399999618530273},{"word":"Hall","start":1.0399999618530273,"end":1.3200000524520874},{"word":"beside","start":2.0999999046325684,"end":2.119999885559082},{"word":"the","start":2.119999885559082,"end":2.619999885559082},{"word":"Exhibition","start":2.619999885559082,"end":3.0799999237060547},{"word":"Road","start":3.0799999237060547,"end":3.3399999141693115},{"word":"entrance","start":3.3399999141693115,"end":3.859999895095825},{"word":"stands","start":4.519999980926514,"end":4.539999961853027},{"word":"a","start":4.539999961853027,"end":4.900000095367432},{"word":"real","start":4.900000095367432,"end":5.360000133514404},{"word":"Stegosaurus","start":5.360000133514404,"end":5.940000057220459},{"word":"skeleton","start":5.940000057220459,"end":6.480000019073486},{"word":"5","start":7.21999979019165,"end":7.400000095367432},{"word":"6","start":7.400000095367432,"end":8.119999885559082},{"word":"metres","start":8.119999885559082,"end":8.420000076293945},{"word":"long","start":8.420000076293945,"end":8.859999656677246},{"word":"with","start":9.279999732971191,"end":9.5},{"word":"big","start":9.5,"end":9.899999618530273},{"word":"plates","start":9.899999618530273,"end":10.2600002288818